    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47787" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλεα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, 
			Lacon.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάλ-</span></b>  (v. infr.), τά, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>good cheer, happy thoughts</i>, of the sleeping Astyanax, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλέων ἐμπλησάμενος κῆρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.504
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν σάλεσσι πολλοῖς ἥμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλέεσσιν ἀνατρέφειν τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
				</span></i>
			<i>Fr. anon.</i><i><span class="en">
				31
			</span></i>.—In form and accent pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλος</span>, in meaning closer to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλεια, θαλία</span>.</div>
